.Dd November 23, 2026
.Dt NETCFG 8
.Os Belka
.Sh NAME
.Nm netcfg
.Nd plumb and configure the IPv4 network
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm plumb
.Nm
.Cm attach
.Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm addr
.Ar interface
.Ar address Ns / Ns Ar length
.Nm
.Cm route add
.Ar destination
.Ar gateway
.Nm
.Cm route delete
.Ar destination
.Op Ar gateway
.Nm
.Cm show
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Belka's network stack is a set of STREAMS multiplexing drivers:
.Pa /dev/ip
for IPv4, ICMP and ARP, with the interfaces' DLPI devices linked below
it, and
.Pa /dev/udp
and
.Pa /dev/tcp ,
each with an IP stream linked below it.
.Nm
makes those links and configures IP.
The links are persistent: they last after
.Nm
exits.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm plumb
Link an IP stream under UDP and under TCP, so that
.Dv AF_INET
sockets can be used.
A transport that is plumbed already is left as it is.
.It Cm attach Ar interface
Make an interface of the DLPI device
.Pa /dev/ Ns Ar interface ,
linking it twice under IP, once for IPv4 and once for ARP.
.It Cm addr Ar interface Ar address Ns / Ns Ar length
Give the interface its address, with a subnet mask of
.Ar length
bits, and a route to the subnet.
.It Cm route add Ar destination Ar gateway
Add a route to
.Ar destination ,
an
.Ar address Ns / Ns Ar length
or
.Cm default ,
by way of
.Ar gateway ,
which must be reachable on an interface.
The longest prefix that matches a datagram's destination is its route.
.It Cm route delete Ar destination Op Ar gateway
Remove that route.
.It Cm show
List the interfaces, the routes and the ARP cache.
.El
.Pp
Changing the configuration needs the superuser.
The loopback interface,
.Li lo0
(127.0.0.1/8), is always there.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/rc.d/network" -compact
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/network
runs
.Nm
at boot, from the settings in
.Xr rc.conf 5 :
.Va network ,
.Va net_interfaces ,
.Va ifaddr_ Ns Ar interface
and
.Va defaultroute .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
QEMU's user-mode network:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
netcfg plumb
netcfg attach vionet0
netcfg addr vionet0 10.0.2.15/24
netcfg route add default 10.0.2.2
.Ed
